The 8B Reviewer found bugs in your cesarops-forge implementation. Apply these fixes and output ONLY the 3 corrected files (llm.rs, tools.rs, loop_engine.rs). The other 4 files (Cargo.toml, main.rs, search.rs, context.rs) are correct â€” do not rewrite them.

BUG 1 â€” llm.rs: KoboldCPP response format is WRONG.
  ACTUAL format: {"results": [{"text": "...generated code..."}]}
  Your code expected: {"text": "..."} â€” WRONG.

  FIX: Change GenerateResponse to:
  `ust
  #[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]
  struct KoboldResult {
      text: String,
  }

  #[derive(Debug, Deserialize)]
  struct GenerateResponse {
      results: Vec<KoboldResult>,
  }
  `
  Then extract: parsed.results.first().map(|r| r.text.clone()).unwrap_or_default()

BUG 2 â€” tools.rs: Return type incompatible with .context()
  PROBLEM: Function returns Result<(), Vec<CompilerError>> but uses .context() which needs anyhow::Error.
  FIX: Split into two parts:
  `ust
  pub fn cargo_check(project_dir: &Path) -> Result<Vec<CompilerError>, anyhow::Error> {
      // Run command, parse JSON, return errors (empty vec = success)
  }
  `
  Caller checks if vec is empty for pass/fail.

  ALSO: cargo --message-format=json output is NESTED:
  {"reason":"compiler-message","message":{"message":"the actual error text","level":"error"}}
  FIX: Check msg.get("reason") == "compiler-message", then msg["message"]["message"] for text, msg["message"]["level"] for level.

BUG 3 â€” loop_engine.rs: commit_files doesn't recurse into subdirectories
  FIX: Add recursive copy helper:
  `ust
  fn copy_dir_recursive(src: &Path, dest: &Path) -> Result<()> {
      fs::create_dir_all(dest)?;
      for entry in fs::read_dir(src)? {
          let entry = entry?;
          let src_path = entry.path();
          let dest_path = dest.join(entry.file_name());
          if src_path.is_dir() {
              copy_dir_recursive(&src_path, &dest_path)?;
          } else {
              fs::copy(&src_path, &dest_path)?;
          }
      }
      Ok(())
  }
  `
  Then commit_files calls copy_dir_recursive(temp_dir, target_dir).

BUG 4 â€” loop_engine.rs: parse_tasks called as loop_engine::parse_tasks but defined in context.rs
  FIX: In loop_engine.rs, add pub use crate::context::parse_tasks; at the top. Or move the function. Simplest: re-export it.

BUG 5 â€” loop_engine.rs: extract_code_blocks regex doesn't match multi-line
  FIX: Add (?s) flag for dot-matches-newline:
  `ust
  let re = Regex::new(r"(?s)`(?:rust)?\s*\n(.*?)\n`").unwrap();
  `
  Also: collect ALL code blocks, not just the first:
  `ust
  fn extract_code_blocks(response: &str) -> Vec<(String, String)> {
      let re = Regex::new(r"(?s)`(?:rust)?\s*\n(.*?)\n`").unwrap();
      re.captures_iter(response)
          .map(|cap| cap.get(1).unwrap().as_str().to_string())
          .collect()
  }
  `

OUTPUT: Three complete corrected files only. Full source, not patches.
1. cesarops-forge/src/llm.rs (with correct KoboldCPP response parsing)
2. cesarops-forge/src/tools.rs (with correct return type + nested JSON parsing)
3. cesarops-forge/src/loop_engine.rs (with recursive copy, re-exported parse_tasks, multi-line regex)

STYLE: anyhow for errors, tracing for logs, no trait objects.
